# Mvir +0, -0, negative and NaN, then a row above Mshock: mass_ratio <= 0.0 takes the no-draw branch (Regime 0, no rand() call) for +0, -0 and the negative Mvir;
# a NaN mass_ratio is not <= 0.0, so the NaN row consumes a draw (queue entry 0) and is classified 0 (u < NaN is false), even with the deviate 0;
# the last row consumes queue entry 1, so the queue order records which rows drew.
# Reachability: constructed routine-domain probe (R4 holds Mvir 0 rows; negative and NaN Mvir are routine-domain states).
